EIH bracket in CM frame equals (3+nu) v^2 + nu (n.v)^2 : True
  -> 1PN interaction (G m1 m2/r)[1 + ((3+nu) v^2 + nu (n.v)^2)/(2c^2)], v = v1 - v2, nu = m1 m2/M^2
m1 v1 - m2 v2 in a frame where the CM moves at V: True   [ = (m1 - m2) V + 2 mu v ]

Galilean-invariant relative momentum k = mu |v1 - v2| (the variable of #11 sec. 8). With p* = 20 keV/c = 1.069e-23 kg m/s,
the equivalent velocity gate v*_pair = p*/mu:
  nucleon-nucleon (mu = m_N/2)    : v*_pair = 1.276e+04 m/s
  electron-electron (mu = m_e/2)  : v*_pair = 2.347e+07 m/s
  1 kg - 1 kg (mu = 0.5 kg)       : v*_pair = 2.138e-23 m/s
  Earth-Moon (mu = 7.2e22 kg)     : v*_pair = 1.482e-46 m/s

Literal variant |m1 v1 - m2 v2| in a frame where the pair's CM moves at V = 370.0 km/s:
  Sun-Earth             : orbital part / boost part = 2 mu v/((m1-m2) V) = 4.83e-07
  Sun-Mars              : orbital part / boost part = 2 mu v/((m1-m2) V) = 4.21e-08
  Earth-Moon            : orbital part / boost part = 2 mu v/((m1-m2) V) = 6.78e-05
  Earth-LAGEOS(407 kg)  : orbital part / boost part = 2 mu v/((m1-m2) V) = 2.10e-24
